Task: Install and record the development tooling (Phase 1, Track foundation-core_20260918)

What was done:
- Confirmed the system Lua interpreter is 5.4.8, the same 5.4 line Aseprite
  embeds, so core modules tested outside the application run on the same
  language semantics they will run on inside it.
- Installed luacheck 1.2.0, luaunit 3.5 and luacov 0.17.0 through LuaRocks into
  the user-local tree at ~/.luarocks (pulling luafilesystem 1.9.0 as a
  dependency, compiled locally against the system Lua headers).
- Installed stylua 2.5.2 as a prebuilt binary into ~/.local/bin rather than
  compiling it, which would have taken minutes for no benefit.
- Verified all four are reachable and that both Lua libraries load.

Files changed:
- conductor/workflow.md (Development Commands section filled in)

Why:
The coverage target and the lint requirement in the process document were
unenforceable without measuring tools. The risk recorded in the track
specification - that coverage tooling might not be installable in this
environment - did not materialise, so the stated target stands unchanged and no
amendment to the process document was needed.

Nothing from this task ships with the extension; it remains dependency-free.
